*unsignal* | V-$CHIPVR ($CHIPCN)

''unsignal(signum)''

Unregisters a signal handler and resets signal to OS default behavior.

*Parameters:*
- ''signum'': Number signal number to unregister (see ''libsignals.chh'')

*Returns:*
- ''ok'' on success (idempotent, succeeds if signal was not registered)

*Supported Signals:*
SIGHUP, SIGINT, SIGQUIT, SIGUSR1, SIGUSR2, SIGPIPE, SIGALRM, SIGTERM, SIGCHLD, SIGCONT, SIGTSTP, SIGTTIN, SIGTTOU, SIGURG, SIGWINCH

*Errors:*
- Runtime error if signum is not a number
- Runtime error if signal number is unsupported
